      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "**The relevant order is MO-25-09-1070, work order ID WO-2025-09-004, for the Cooler Plate Pack at Modine’s Racine operation.** I verified its September Pending Close cutoff, but the cost-event records needed to complete the review were unavailable.\n\n| Review item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Cost period | Sep-25 (`PER-COST-2025-09`) |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **`2025-09-30T18:00:00`** |\n| Source transaction ID | Cannot verify—event ledger unavailable |\n| Event amount | Cannot verify |\n| Exact event-created time | Cannot verify |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Cannot verify |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Undetermined** |\n\nThe supplied public records contain work orders and cost periods but **no cost-event rows**. The supporting event input repeatedly returned “Supporting input was not staged for this assignment.” Authorized shared work products also lacked the transaction, timestamp, and status details required. This is **not evidence that no late event occurred**.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B states that newly created transactions falling in the Pending Close period or an earlier period are **not staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened**. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing.\n\nTherefore, assessing consistency requires the event’s creation timestamp, type, and recorded status; I cannot responsibly conclude consistency or inconsistency without them.\n\n*Source: “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233, printed page 225.*\n\n**No database records were changed.** The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_f867719b22ff/audit-report.json`; the submitted report remains marked **needs evidence**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
